text+=['\n### Score availability\n',table(['cohort','signature','operator','available / attempted','reason','gene-level reference audit'],status)]
text+=['All attempted operators and sample denominators remain in the status and full pairwise matrices. Non-unanimity is calculated across available operators, with the available panel reported per signature/cohort; percentages from panels of different sizes are not directly interchangeable. `results/*_scores.csv` and `*_research_groups.csv` retain sample-level scores/calls locally.']
text+=['\n## B2-primary and uncertainty\n','Two prespecified headline contrasts are in the first table. The complete 7×7 disagreement matrix per signature/cohort, Spearman correlations, median and 90th-percentile absolute rank displacement (100 × absolute difference in average tied ranks / n, percentage points), unavailable entries and attempted denominators are in `results/*_pairwise_metrics.csv`. High means score ≥ cohort median, R quantile type 7, ties high; no numerical threshold is transported from first-line trials.','Intervals use 2,000 fixed-score paired bootstrap draws, seed 20261113, with medians recomputed within each draw. TRACERx resamples patients and retains all their regions; region-level estimands remain region-weighted. Other cohorts resample patients/cases. Operators and reference parameters are not refit within bootstrap draws, as permitted by the plan; intervals are conditional on fitted scores. Complete operator recomputation would multiply the saved full-panel runtime by 2,000 and was not used.']
text+=['\n## B2-TRACERx multiregion — exploratory\n',table(['signature','operator','patients with ≥2 regions','discordant patients','discordance % (exact 95% CI)','source'],[[r['signature'],r['operator'],r['n_multiregion'],r['discordant_patients'] or 'unavailable',f(r['discordance_percent'])+' ('+ci(r['lower'],r['upper'])+')',src('TRACERx_within_patient_discordance.csv')] for r in read('TRACERx_within_patient_discordance.csv')])]
text+=['Patient discordance means at least one retained region on each side of that operator’s full regional-cohort median. Patients, not regions, are the binomial units. Region operator disagreement and how often one region changes research group are the TRACERx primary pairwise/non-unanimity rows above.']
text+=[table(['signature','operator','between-patient variance','within-patient variance','ICC'],[[r['signature'],r['operator'],f(r['between_patient_variance'],5),f(r['within_patient_variance'],5),f(r['ICC'],3)] for r in read('TRACERx_variance_ICC.csv')])]
text+=['Variance components use a REML patient random-intercept model on all retained regions. Variances depend on each score’s units; ICC is the between/(between+within) fraction. No ICC CI was prespecified; no interval is invented. Source: '+src('TRACERx_variance_ICC.csv')+'.']
one=read('TRACERx_one_region_pairwise_metrics.csv')
text+=['\n### One randomly selected region per patient — sensitivity\n','One region was selected independently of outcomes using seed 20261113, retaining 79 patients (`TRACERx_one_region_selection.csv`). All operators/references were recomputed in this 79-region matrix; the nominated selection was not replaced when a reference failed. Angio36 O2/O3/O7 may therefore be unavailable even when full-cohort scores are available.']
text+=[table(['signature','contrast','n','disagreement %','95% CI'],[[r['signature'],r['operator_a']+' vs '+r['operator_b'],r['n_total'],f(r['disagreement_percent']),ci(r['lower'],r['upper'])] for r in one if r['operator_a']=='O1' and r['operator_b'] in ['O2','O5']])]
text+=['Complete sensitivity outputs: `TRACERx_one_region_pairwise_metrics.csv`, `TRACERx_one_region_nonunanimous.csv`, `TRACERx_one_region_operator_status.csv`.']
text+=['\n## B2-CM025 clinical — exploratory, separate later-line trial\n','The treatment-stratified five-fold partition with seed 20261113 was saved **before the first outcome fit** to `../shared/CM025_folds.csv`; its SHA256 and timestamps are recorded in the reproduction CSV. Each fold contains 24 nivolumab and 26 everolimus patients. This nominated partition is reused without reselection. Baseline RNA selection and event=1 coding are inherited from the source-qualified CM025 contract.']
text+=[table(['signature','available / attempted','reclassified patients','per 100 (exact 95% CI)'],[[r['signature'],r['n_available']+'/'+r['n_total'],r['reclassified_n'],f(r['reclassified_per_100'])+' ('+ci(r['lower'],r['upper'])+')'] for r in read('CM025_frozen_reclassification.csv')])]
text+=['Source: `CM025_frozen_reclassification.csv`; held-out scores, training medians, signed distances to each frozen threshold and all four I0→I1 transition groups are in `CM025_frozen_scores_transitions.csv`. These intervals condition on the nominated fitted references and do not propagate training variability.']
text+=[table(['signature','endpoint','operator','n / events','interaction HR (95% CI)','Wald p','BH q'],[[r['signature'],r['endpoint'],r['operator'],r['n']+' / '+r['events'],f(r['estimate'],3)+' ('+ci(r['lower'],r['upper'],3)+')',f(r['p'],4),f(r['BH_q'],4)] for r in read('CM025_interactions.csv')])]
text+=['Source: `CM025_interactions.csv`. PFS is the primary endpoint within B2-CM025; OS is secondary. Constant Cox model: `Surv(time,event) ~ score_per_SD + APM12 + treatment + APM12:treatment + score:treatment`, Efron ties. APM12 is the existing gene-standardised, aggregate-standardised 12-gene comparator. Treatment=1 is nivolumab, 0 everolimus; an interaction HR >1 means the relative nivolumab-versus-everolimus HR increases per SD higher score. BH correction is within signature×endpoint across the operator panel; null/unfavourable results are retained. PH interaction diagnostics are included in the CSV.']
ph=[r for r in read('CM025_interactions.csv') if math.isfinite(num(r['PH_interaction_p'])) and num(r['PH_interaction_p'])<.05]
text+=['Every estimable PFS and OS interaction 95% CI includes 1. '+('The prespecified constant interaction summary has a nominal PH diagnostic <0.05 for '+', '.join(r['signature']+' '+r['operator']+' '+r['endpoint']+' (p='+f(r['PH_interaction_p'],4)+')' for r in ph)+'. This limits a constant-HR interpretation; no outcome-driven alternative model was selected.' if ph else 'No nominal interaction PH diagnostic is below 0.05.')]
text+=[table(['arm','patients','PFS events','OS events','ORR evaluable','responders'],[[r[k] for k in ['arm','n','PFS_events','OS_events','ORR_evaluable','responders']] for r in read('CM025_endpoint_denominators.csv')])]
text+=['For both signatures and each randomised arm, `CM025_transition_survival.csv` reports all four transition groups plus an explicit unavailable category: attempted/evaluable n, PFS/OS events, KM median and 95% CI, 12-month PFS/OS and log-log 95% CI, numbers at risk and 12-month RMST. `CM025_transition_ORR.csv` reports CR/PR successes, evaluable n, NE/missing n, ORR and exact 95% CI. Empty cells remain non-estimable. If KM survival reaches zero before month 12, its zero tail is retained for the 12-month point and RMST; the log-log CI may remain undefined. Otherwise follow-up support to month 12 is required. No nonzero survival tail is extrapolated. These are descriptive subgroup outcomes, not individual treatment-benefit estimates.']
text+=['\n## B2-CPTAC four-protein anchor — exploratory supporting context\n','The existing proxy is the equal mean of gene-wise z-standardised log2 protein ratios for CDH5, ENG, PCDH12 and SPARCL1, with protein reference fitted in the 78 complete cases. Scores use the full 109-case RNA cohort references, then are correlated within the 78 paired cases. The 2,000 paired case-bootstrap draws preserve the RNA-score/proxy pairing; score and protein references are fixed. Small sample size, prior resource exposure, heterogeneous sample-label linkage and absence of randomised treatment limit interpretation.']
text+=[table(['signature','operator','n','Spearman rho (95% CI)','rho difference vs O1 (paired 95% CI)'],[[r['signature'],r['operator'],r['n'],f(r['spearman'],3)+' ('+ci(r['lower'],r['upper'],3)+')',f(r['difference_vs_O1'],3)+' ('+ci(r['difference_lower'],r['difference_upper'],3)+')'] for r in read('CPTAC_protein_anchor.csv')])]
text+=['Source: `CPTAC_protein_anchor.csv`; proxy values in `CPTAC_protein_proxy.csv`. This is an independent measurement modality supporting molecular context, not a vascular gold standard, histology/IHC match or treatment-benefit validation.']
text+=['\n## Reproducibility, checks and resource use\n','Run order and commands are in `scripts/README.md`. Full intermediates (>50 MB) are exclusively in `/LOCAL_EXTERNAL_DRIVE/MacBook_Project_Storage/JCO_PO_Upgrade_scratch_20261113/B2/`. Final nominated analysis runs use serial GSVA and one R data.table thread, with no more than two active B2 computational processes. `R_MAX_VSIZE=3Gb` is a heap guard; measured RSS/footprint is recorded in `results/resource_usage.csv` and time logs. The initial readxl parser had an excessive transient footprint; it was replaced with exact streaming XML extraction (no gene/sample reduction), while complete primary analyses were retained. Final streamed preparation and cohort runs have separate logs. No system library was changed.','Validation checks: `results/validation_checks.csv`; common synthetic operator parity and singscore toy: `operator_synthetic_parity.csv`, `singscore_toy_check.csv`. Source ledgers and output SHA256 manifests accompany the run. Diagnostic plot only: `diagnostics/B2_primary_comparisons.html`; final manuscript figures are outside B2 scope.']
text+=['\n## What was not run and why\n','- O3 Angio36 is reported unavailable wherever any required reference MAD is ≤1e−8; the failure is methodological/reference support, not compute failure. See all operator-status and signature-reference-QC tables.','- The one-region TRACERx sensitivity retains its zero-SD/MAD failures; no alternative region was selected to restore availability.','- Operators were not refit in each bootstrap: the plan explicitly permits fixed-score intervals when full recomputation runtime is impractical. All primary point estimates and the one-region sensitivity were run in full.','- No frozen O6 single-patient analysis: GSVA has no natural frozen form; §3 requires frozen held-out O1/O2 only, both completed.','- No matched histology/IHC analysis: physical-slide/RNA correspondence remains unqualified and this is outside the locked B2 estimands.','- KM median upper limits or fixed-horizon outcomes without follow-up support are non-estimable where indicated; these are data limitations, not null scores or compute failures.','- No treatment inference in TCGA/CPTAC and no pooling of later-line CM025 with first-line trials. No required primary analysis remains blocked by compute, missing data or access.']
text+=['\n## What this does and does not show\n','- The same expression data can yield different research high/low groups under prespecified score operators in other renal patients/platforms.','- Multiregion results quantify specimen dependence with patient-level inference; regional sampling and arithmetic both contribute.','- The CM025 endpoint models and transition groups remain exploratory, later-line and treatment-specific; no individual benefit is identified.','- CPTAC supplies supporting protein context, not a universal biological truth or assay calibration.','- All resources have prior project exposure; this is replication of the phenomenon, not untouched or prospective validation.','- Cohort-specific medians test recurrence of disagreement; they do not transport a first-line trial numerical threshold.']
